                <pb facs="0250" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg144"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr. Egan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 112.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 153, of April 21
                    last, stating that the Chilean Government was desirous of purchasing a war
                    vessel from the United States, I have to inform you that the Navy Department
                    replies that it has none for sale.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
